Date: Thu, 5 Feb 2026 12:51:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] multi-vendor: Add QCA vendor-specific TLV support to
 prplMesh

Integrate QCA as a vendor in the multi-vendor framework, enabling
QCA-specific TLV handling in IEEE 1905.1 messages.

Implementation details:
- Added MultiVendorQCA class that registers QCA vendor handlers and parsers
- Implemented QCA version info TLV (v1.0.0) for AP autoconfiguration messages
- Added send-side handler: add_qca_version_info_tlv()
- Added receive-side parser: parse_qca_vs_tlv() with TLV ID routing
- Proper endianness handling with local copy byte swapping before validation

Architecture:
- Uses direct registration API: register_handler() and register_parser()
- OUI validation performed in parser using local buffer copies
- Parser creates local copies of OUI and TLV ID, swaps bytes, then validates
- Only consumes TLV buffer after successful OUI/ID validation
- Thread-safe registration with static initialization

QCA TLV structure:
- Vendor OUI: QCA_OUI (0x001374)
- TLV ID: QCA_VERSION_INFO
- Payload: version_major, version_minor, version_patch

This implementation follows the vendor example pattern and integrates
seamlessly with the multi-vendor framework's parser iterator mechanism.

Signed-off-by: Vignesh Sridharan <vignsrid@qti.qualcomm.com>
